# <%= current_page.data.title %>

Jenkins uses GitHub App credentials to scan HMCTS repositories, retrieve seed-job configuration, and load shared libraries. Credentials are managed in [CNP Flux](https://github.com/hmcts/cnp-flux-config/blob/master/apps/jenkins/jenkins/jenkins.yaml). Do not include private keys or token values in this runbook.

## Instances

The shared Jenkins configuration is included by both CFT instances:

- CFT PTL: `ptl-intsvc`
- CFT PTL Sandbox: `sbox-intsvc`

## App usage

| Jenkins credential | Jenkins functionality | Instances |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `hmcts-jenkins-a-to-c` | Authenticates the A-C HMCTS organization-folder scans, including the nightly folder. | CFT PTL and CFT Sandbox |
| `hmcts-jenkins-d-to-i` | Authenticates the D-I HMCTS organization-folder scans, including the nightly folder. | CFT PTL and CFT Sandbox |
| `hmcts-jenkins-j-to-z` | Authenticates the J-Z HMCTS organization-folder scans, including the nightly folder. | CFT PTL and CFT Sandbox |
| `hmcts-jenkins-cnp` | Checks out the Jenkins seed-job configuration and retrieves the `Infrastructure`, `Pipeline`, and `Tagged` shared libraries from `cnp-jenkins-library`. | CFT PTL and CFT Sandbox |
| `hmcts-jenkins-cft` | Authenticates the sandbox-only `Pipeline_Test` organization scan for configured CNP Plum, Rhubarb, and Jenkins-library repositories. | CFT Sandbox |
| `hmcts-jenkins-rpe` | No consumer is identified in the current Jenkins configuration or organization DSL. Confirm its purpose with the Jenkins or GitHub App owner. | Credential is provisioned, but no consumer is found in the configuration |

The organization-folder scans use GitHub to discover eligible repositories, branches, and pull requests. Repositories are filtered using the approved-repository list and configured topic or name filters.

